From afe00a70a32d19a3dbbbedd93ed0f6c43e751d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Panagiotis Georgakopoulos <8681967+pankgeorg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:36:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] cmake: build for WASI

Define NO_MMAP for `CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME` WASI: WASI preview 1 has no `mmap`
(wasi-libc offers only an emulation behind `_WASI_EMULATED_MMAN`), so
packfiles and other mapped files are read into allocated memory, as on other
platforms without mmap.

With the preceding changes, libgit2 builds for wasm32-wasip1 with wasi-sdk's
toolchain file and

    cmake -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=<wasi-sdk>/share/cmake/wasi-sdk-p1.cmake \
          -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_CLI=OFF \
          -DUSE_THREADS=OFF -DUSE_HTTPS=OFF -DUSE_SSH=OFF

Network access needs a custom transport or stream, since WASI preview 1 has
no sockets.
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 73c46e2..fe128f0 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -154,6 +154,11 @@ if(AMIGA)
 	add_definitions(-DNO_ADDRINFO -DNO_READDIR_R -DNO_MMAP)
 endif()
 
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "WASI")
+	# WASI preview 1 has no mmap (packs are read into memory instead)
+	add_definitions(-DNO_MMAP)
+endif()
+
 # threads
 
 if(USE_THREADS)
